1
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:06,950
<i>This intensity... It's just like Eris!</i>

2
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:08,640
<i>She's a Hyral Menas!</i>

3
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:09,770
Get 'em!

4
00:00:11,470 --> 00:00:16,250
<i>Truly fortune favors me, that a Hyral Menas should be among my opponents!</i>

5
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:20,040
<i>Could there be any better way 
to test the fruits of my training?</i>

6
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:23,450
You're a Hyral Menas, right?

7
00:00:23,450 --> 00:00:25,330
A Hyral Menas?

8
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:29,220
Rani, protect Seilyn and the others.

9
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:31,290
I'll handle her!

10
00:00:31,290 --> 00:00:33,010
Y-Yeah...

11
00:00:33,010 --> 00:00:36,680
You sure do look happy at times like these.

12
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:38,540
Oh, you can tell?

13
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:40,870
You're grinning from ear to ear.

14
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:42,350
A-Am I?

15
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:44,870
Anyway, keep them all safe, okay?

16
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:46,020
Got it!

17
00:00:46,450 --> 00:00:48,730
I ask that you fight me instead.

18
00:00:48,730 --> 00:00:50,680
Is this some kind of joke?

19
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:54,190
A weak girl like you 
stands no chance against me.

20
00:00:56,180 --> 00:00:58,670
<i>Now, I'll just convert my aether to mana...</i>

21
00:01:00,010 --> 00:01:00,990
What?

22
00:01:18,050 --> 00:01:21,010
<u>Reborn</u>

23
00:01:18,050 --> 00:01:21,010
to Master the Blade
     From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

24
00:01:18,050 --> 00:01:21,010
to Master the Blade
From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

25
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:39,010
Episode 4    The Town Ruled by the Highlander

26
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:36,090
<i>Impossible...</i>

27
00:02:36,670 --> 00:02:39,590
<i>Inglis's mana is this strong?</i>

28
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:44,030
Burst! Shiny Flow!

29
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:55,290
Please don't hold back.

30
00:02:55,290 --> 00:02:56,310
Very well.

31
00:02:56,580 --> 00:03:01,520
I've been bored lately without 
any good foes to fight.

32
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:04,600
<i>She's so aggressive! I love it!</i>

33
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:07,540
<i>I'm liking her more and more by the second!</i>

34
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:09,130
I think we'll get along.

35
00:03:09,130 --> 00:03:11,750
I was just thinking the same thing.

36
00:03:11,750 --> 00:03:14,890
Bratty little girl...

37
00:03:14,890 --> 00:03:16,760
Draw your sword.

38
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:17,790
That won't be necessary.

39
00:03:17,790 --> 00:03:18,710
What?

40
00:03:19,010 --> 00:03:20,800
It's uselessly dull.

41
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:26,310
Time to find out if your words are true.

42
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:35,530
An ordinary knight would've been run through 
before they could move a muscle.

43
00:03:36,050 --> 00:03:38,730
Of course, if you couldn't dodge 
this much, it'd be no fun at all!

44
00:03:41,970 --> 00:03:45,590
<i>She's maintaining her distance at all times, 
even as she attacks with her spear!</i>

45
00:03:46,370 --> 00:03:47,360
<i>Very good!</i>

46
00:03:50,090 --> 00:03:54,540
<i>She keeps closing the distance 
with each attack I make.</i>

47
00:03:56,600 --> 00:03:58,470
You're out of room to fall back.

48
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:03,280
Nice attack!

49
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:07,470
Mine wasn't half bad either.

50
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:16,390
<i>Very good. She's strong enough to stand up 
right after a hit like that.</i>

51
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:21,150
<i>And her desire to fight hasn't dulled at all!</i>

52
00:04:21,150 --> 00:04:22,600
<i>Excellent!</i>

53
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:26,230
You have so much power.

54
00:04:26,230 --> 00:04:28,820
Why are you serving a Highlander?

55
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:31,940
Her kind are trying 
to steal away the surface.

56
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:35,990
You're not just letting that happen. 
You're actively helping them.

57
00:04:35,990 --> 00:04:39,810
Well, Lady Seilyn seems nice.

58
00:04:39,810 --> 00:04:42,660
And the people in town seemed to like her.

59
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:46,140
If you only look at what's 
happening on the surface, sure.

60
00:04:46,380 --> 00:04:47,700
Surface?

61
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:50,220
You didn't notice something 
wrong about the town?

62
00:04:50,550 --> 00:04:53,240
The flow of mana?

63
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:55,180
What about it?

64
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:58,140
If you noticed, then look into it yourself.

65
00:04:58,140 --> 00:05:01,850
And realize for yourself 
how foolish your deeds are.

66
00:05:01,850 --> 00:05:04,110
I'd be lying if I said 
I wasn't a bit curious.

67
00:05:04,650 --> 00:05:09,030
But unfortunately, 
I'm not here to play hero!

68
00:05:09,450 --> 00:05:14,490
I was just helping her to earn some money 
after we ate too much and spent it all.

69
00:05:14,490 --> 00:05:16,100
To earn money?

70
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:18,450
And thanks to that, I got to fight you!

71
00:05:18,450 --> 00:05:21,140
So I'm grateful to all that food I ate.

72
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:24,750
What use is power without justice?

73
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:27,710
I get to have fun! That's all!

74
00:05:27,710 --> 00:05:29,260
Fool!

75
00:05:30,170 --> 00:05:34,060
I refuse to let somebody 
like you have such power!

76
00:05:39,430 --> 00:05:41,120
You did well to dodge that.

77
00:05:41,650 --> 00:05:44,580
<i>An attack that ignores space and distance...</i>

78
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:47,120
<i>So this is her true, hidden power.</i>

79
00:05:48,050 --> 00:05:49,540
<i>Now this is getting interesting!</i>

80
00:05:55,210 --> 00:05:56,800
She keeps moving around...

81
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:01,090
<i>I've been waiting for this!</i>

82
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:04,450
So, what will you do now?

83
00:06:04,450 --> 00:06:07,590
Fool! You've also stopped moving!

84
00:06:08,610 --> 00:06:10,750
<i>So she can kick, not just use her spear?</i>

85
00:06:11,430 --> 00:06:13,300
<i>She knew what I'd do, too...</i>

86
00:06:15,590 --> 00:06:17,310
Now you're mine!

87
00:06:19,970 --> 00:06:21,320
What?

88
00:06:27,190 --> 00:06:29,370
That was a good fight, huh?

89
00:06:29,370 --> 00:06:31,920
I had more fun than I thought I would.

90
00:06:35,630 --> 00:06:38,940
How will I ever face them now?

91
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,200
Chris!

92
00:06:40,690 --> 00:06:42,970
I dealt with the enemies outside!

93
00:06:45,410 --> 00:06:46,930
Chris...

94
00:06:46,930 --> 00:06:48,180
Rani!

95
00:06:48,180 --> 00:06:51,880
I can't let myself be captured here.

96
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:56,170
Let me go, if you value her life.

97
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:59,360
Chris...

98
00:07:01,330 --> 00:07:03,980
Go, then.

99
00:07:05,980 --> 00:07:08,350
But may I say one thing?

100
00:07:09,150 --> 00:07:12,490
You're free to do whatever 
you want when fighting me.

101
00:07:12,490 --> 00:07:16,040
Flee as many times as you like, 
if you think things aren't going your way.

102
00:07:17,420 --> 00:07:21,530
However, if you ever hurt Rani again...

103
00:07:22,290 --> 00:07:24,600
You're a dead woman.

104
00:07:26,190 --> 00:07:27,640
That's all.

105
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,460
Have a nice evening.

106
00:07:29,460 --> 00:07:31,220
What's your name?

107
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:33,680
Inglis Eucus.

108
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:35,340
A pleasure to make your acquaintance.

109
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:37,280
Sistia Rouge.

110
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:38,520
Until we meet again...

111
00:07:42,710 --> 00:07:43,980
Rani!

112
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:45,370
Are you okay?

113
00:07:47,010 --> 00:07:48,140
I'm okay.

114
00:07:49,050 --> 00:07:50,400
Sorry...

115
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:52,330
I guess I interrupted you.

116
00:07:52,330 --> 00:07:55,120
No, I was done.

117
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:57,150
So were you, right?

118
00:07:57,150 --> 00:07:58,190
Yes.

119
00:07:58,190 --> 00:08:00,490
Lady Seilyn's safe.

120
00:08:00,490 --> 00:08:02,470
Our mission's complete.

121
00:08:02,470 --> 00:08:03,920
Yup.

122
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:09,000
Thank you so much for your help yesterday.

123
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:13,530
Thanks to you, none of my men were injured.

124
00:08:13,530 --> 00:08:15,710
I'm glad we could help.

125
00:08:15,710 --> 00:08:19,930
Are the former knights we captured 
going to be executed?

126
00:08:20,210 --> 00:08:25,220
No, they were once loyal 
servants of this city.

127
00:08:25,770 --> 00:08:28,470
They simply got a little arrogant.

128
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:32,600
I want them to change their ways and 
use their strength not for themselves,

129
00:08:32,940 --> 00:08:37,300
but for the weak and powerless.

130
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:40,570
I plan on taking my time 
to persuade them of this.

131
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:46,320
And if they're willing to change, 
I'm going to hire them again.

132
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:49,670
Wow! And to think they tried to kill you!

133
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,700
I think that's wonderful.

134
00:08:55,550 --> 00:08:58,320
Oh? This has an unusual taste.

135
00:08:58,320 --> 00:09:03,550
Yes. I thought you might be tired from 
yesterday, so I've added some herbs to it.

136
00:09:03,550 --> 00:09:04,960
I see.

137
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:09,320
I do feel relaxed, 
like I could sleep very well.

138
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:11,440
Yes, it's good.

139
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,740
It is.

140
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:20,380
There's something I want 
to talk to you about.

141
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:22,280
Will you come with me?

142
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:23,400
Y-Yes?

143
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:27,620
I didn't realize there was a place 
like this under the castle.

144
00:09:28,330 --> 00:09:30,850
Only a select few know of it.

145
00:09:32,970 --> 00:09:34,410
That's...

146
00:09:39,890 --> 00:09:44,430
This magic circle is draining away mana.

147
00:09:44,430 --> 00:09:48,220
Lady Seilyn... What is this?

148
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:53,380
The core of the Highland. 
A Levitation Circle.

149
00:09:54,130 --> 00:09:58,620
It absorbs mana from its surroundings, 
and when it has enough,

150
00:09:58,620 --> 00:10:02,780
it breaks the land away from the earth 
around it and brings it to the sky.

151
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:03,970
The sky?

152
00:10:03,970 --> 00:10:06,100
Does that mean...?

153
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:08,490
It will become a new Highland.

154
00:10:08,490 --> 00:10:11,680
Her kind are trying 
to steal away the surface.

155
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:15,510
<i>I thought she meant in the
political or psychological sense.</i>

156
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:19,390
<i>I didn't think she literally meant they 
were stealing the surface itself...</i>

157
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,500
If it flies up into the sky,

158
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:25,060
what happens to the people who live here?

159
00:10:25,690 --> 00:10:29,170
The Highland is for Highlanders.

160
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:33,310
They'll either have to leave or become 
slaves of Highlanders themselves.

161
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:37,710
I'm planning on asking the higher-ups 
to let those who wish live here

162
00:10:37,710 --> 00:10:41,920
without becoming slaves, or even allow them 
to become Highlanders themselves.

163
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:43,790
Can you do that?

164
00:10:44,310 --> 00:10:47,480
I will. Even if I have to fight the Highland.

165
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:51,350
Why are you telling us 
something so important?

166
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:55,600
Because I wanted somebody 
to forgive me, I guess.

167
00:10:56,450 --> 00:11:02,470
My being here as this city's ruler 
means it may someday be destroyed.

168
00:11:03,010 --> 00:11:09,470
But I'm hiding that from everyone... 
and I don't know if that's okay.

169
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:12,440
So I want to ask you...

170
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:15,250
Is it okay for me to be here?

171
00:11:15,790 --> 00:11:20,110
If not, you may strike me down where I stand.

172
00:11:20,790 --> 00:11:23,780
C-Chris, what do we say?

173
00:11:24,030 --> 00:11:27,610
She's asking you for your opinion.

174
00:11:28,090 --> 00:11:30,750
You need to tell her what you think.

175
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:33,710
What about you, Chris?

176
00:11:33,710 --> 00:11:37,710
Me? I'll go with whatever you say.

177
00:11:37,710 --> 00:11:39,920
I'm going to be your squire, after all.

178
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:41,790
That's not fair!

179
00:11:41,790 --> 00:11:44,330
That's what it means to be the boss!

180
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:46,380
Okay...

181
00:11:46,770 --> 00:11:48,390
Lady Seilyn...

182
00:11:49,730 --> 00:11:52,740
I want to believe in you.

183
00:11:52,740 --> 00:11:57,020
Because I think you believe what you say.

184
00:11:57,630 --> 00:11:59,040
Rafinha...

185
00:11:59,410 --> 00:12:06,490
When this land takes flight, if you 
need my power, I'll come to help you.

186
00:12:06,770 --> 00:12:11,360
I'm going to train at the knights' academy 
in the capital and study hard!

187
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:13,960
I'll be able to help you more then!

188
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:18,090
So when that happens, 
take me on as a knight here!

189
00:12:19,090 --> 00:12:22,550
Thank you, Rafinha...

190
00:12:24,610 --> 00:12:26,580
This is okay, right, Chris?

191
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:29,230
It's what I've decided for myself.

192
00:12:29,230 --> 00:12:31,150
It's fine.

193
00:12:31,150 --> 00:12:34,860
If things go well, we might get 
to fight a Highlander army!

194
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:37,800
That's not going well at all!

195
00:12:58,870 --> 00:13:01,140
What was that? An earthquake?

196
00:13:01,140 --> 00:13:02,770
I heard voices from this direction!

197
00:13:02,770 --> 00:13:04,340
Be careful, Rani!

198
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,270
A magicite beast!

199
00:13:17,220 --> 00:13:18,490
That's...

200
00:13:18,950 --> 00:13:22,330
No... Is that Lady Seilyn?

201
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:25,910
Why? There hasn't been any Prism Flow!

202
00:13:25,910 --> 00:13:29,850
Rani, remember what 
happened three years ago.

203
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:31,270
Three years ago?

204
00:13:35,070 --> 00:13:40,890
Rahl was turned into a magicite beast 
by the Bloodchain Brigade's Prism Powder.

205
00:13:40,890 --> 00:13:44,390
So this is the Bloodchain Brigade again?

206
00:13:44,390 --> 00:13:45,970
The question is... when?

207
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:52,170
Pathetic!

208
00:13:52,170 --> 00:13:54,890
Now begone, Highlander!

209
00:13:55,210 --> 00:13:56,550
Mimoza?!

210
00:14:01,850 --> 00:14:03,820
So <i>that's</i> where the Prism Powder was?

211
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:08,150
My son was killed by a Highlander!

212
00:14:08,730 --> 00:14:11,120
Go to hell!

213
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:20,660
Magicite beasts! Split up!

214
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:21,850
Wait!

215
00:14:22,350 --> 00:14:24,640
You need to evacuate the people in the castle!

216
00:14:24,970 --> 00:14:25,920
But...

217
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:28,060
Leave this to us! Hurry!

218
00:14:28,060 --> 00:14:29,100
Understood.

219
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:31,300
What do we do, Chris?

220
00:14:31,550 --> 00:14:33,140
We have to stop her.

221
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:36,380
Rani, if she looks like she's going to fire 
another one of those beams, block her!

222
00:14:36,810 --> 00:14:37,890
Got it!

223
00:14:43,140 --> 00:14:45,500
Lady Seilyn, stop this, please!

224
00:14:49,030 --> 00:14:50,850
No, Lady Seilyn!

225
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:16,170
You're...

226
00:15:16,170 --> 00:15:17,380
Die!

227
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:19,600
Stop it!

228
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:23,530
Don't interfere! 
I didn't come here to fight you!

229
00:15:23,790 --> 00:15:26,850
You're with the Bloodchain 
Brigade, aren't you?

230
00:15:26,850 --> 00:15:29,440
And what if I am?

231
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:35,660
If I'd defeated you then, Mimoza wouldn't 
have gotten her hands on the Prism Powder.

232
00:15:35,660 --> 00:15:37,810
No, that's not true.

233
00:15:38,840 --> 00:15:43,320
My comrades all carry Prism Powder.

234
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:45,870
Comrade Mimoza already had it.

235
00:15:45,870 --> 00:15:47,290
<i>When did he show up?</i>

236
00:15:48,070 --> 00:15:53,110
The plan to use the banished knights 
to attack the Highlander failed.

237
00:15:53,110 --> 00:15:56,180
So Comrade Mimoza took action on her own.

238
00:15:56,180 --> 00:15:57,560
And who might you be?

239
00:15:57,560 --> 00:16:00,680
I am the leader of the Bloodchain Brigade.

240
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:03,690
I have no name. Call me what you like.

241
00:16:04,420 --> 00:16:07,140
I've come to protect this land.

242
00:16:07,750 --> 00:16:11,620
From the danger that you people created?

243
00:16:11,620 --> 00:16:16,580
We will eliminate the Highlander, 
but the people of this land are innocent.

244
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:18,780
I won't let you hurt either of them.

245
00:16:20,970 --> 00:16:23,390
Chris! We need to stop her!

246
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:26,510
Get out of here.

247
00:16:28,230 --> 00:16:29,540
I won't let you!

248
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:47,560
<i>I didn't think anyone could take a clean hit 
from my Aether-Shell-enhanced fist.</i>

249
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:50,610
<i>It seems I still have much 
to see of the world!</i>

250
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:52,150
Step aside!

251
00:16:52,150 --> 00:16:54,790
Sorry, but I can't.

252
00:16:57,410 --> 00:16:58,840
<i>Amazing!</i>

253
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:03,250
<i>I'd love to have a nice, long fight 
with him, but now's not the time!</i>

254
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:08,090
You're mine.

255
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,920
Not on my watch!

256
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:16,580
Then I'll take you out first!

257
00:17:16,580 --> 00:17:18,880
Lady Seilyn!

258
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:22,100
Lady Seilyn, are you okay?

259
00:17:22,370 --> 00:17:24,050
Are you hurt?

260
00:17:24,050 --> 00:17:28,020
Are you in pain, Lady Seilyn?

261
00:17:28,020 --> 00:17:29,990
No! Sistia!

262
00:17:29,990 --> 00:17:30,750
Yes!

263
00:17:31,630 --> 00:17:33,700
Lady Seilyn!

264
00:17:32,050 --> 00:17:33,180
Run!

265
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:35,100
What's wrong?

266
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:37,450
Are you okay?

267
00:17:37,450 --> 00:17:39,360
Lady Seilyn?

268
00:17:40,290 --> 00:17:41,360
That's...

269
00:17:41,830 --> 00:17:43,980
Lady Seilyn!

270
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:45,440
No!

271
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:53,130
Lady Seilyn, no!

272
00:18:02,130 --> 00:18:03,240
Chris!

273
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:06,840
What are you doing? 
You should've allowed her a clean death!

274
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:10,460
Lady Seilyn is still in there!

275
00:18:10,460 --> 00:18:13,030
We can't let her die!

276
00:18:13,030 --> 00:18:15,750
But nothing's changed.

277
00:18:16,330 --> 00:18:18,280
There's something I want to try.

278
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:20,620
Distract her.

279
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:24,280
If I fail, I'll let you do as you like.

280
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:28,360
Very well. Let's make a deal.

281
00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:34,000
Whether this works or not, 
when it's over, you leave the city.

282
00:18:34,330 --> 00:18:37,130
We're going to destroy 
the Levitation Circle,

283
00:18:37,130 --> 00:18:40,050
and I don't want you trying to interfere.

284
00:18:40,050 --> 00:18:41,640
Very well.

285
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:45,220
I'm sorry I won't get a chance to fight you.

286
00:18:45,220 --> 00:18:47,230
Now, if you'll excuse me.

287
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:49,760
We have a deal.

288
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:52,440
Sistia, distract her!

289
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:53,920
Understood!

290
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:55,130
You too, Rani!

291
00:18:55,130 --> 00:18:56,240
Got it.

292
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:59,720
Chris, make sure you stop 
Lady Seilyn, all right?

293
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:01,860
Yeah, I'll give it my best shot!

294
00:19:14,970 --> 00:19:17,600
<i>Firstly, I convert all of 
my aether into mana.</i>

295
00:19:24,470 --> 00:19:28,430
<i>I control it and shift into 
casting a spell...</i>

296
00:19:28,430 --> 00:19:31,020
<i>I'm ready to cast!</i>

297
00:19:34,730 --> 00:19:39,780
Freeze!

298
00:19:52,650 --> 00:19:53,700
Oh?

299
00:19:56,210 --> 00:19:58,430
Chris, are you okay?

300
00:19:58,430 --> 00:20:00,920
Yeah, I think it worked.

301
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:06,380
Hey, Lady Seilyn's okay, right?

302
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:09,410
Yeah, magicite beasts are tough to kill.

303
00:20:09,410 --> 00:20:12,010
I think she'll be able 
to move when it melts.

304
00:20:12,010 --> 00:20:13,220
Good...

305
00:20:13,220 --> 00:20:16,110
But we need to get her away from here.

306
00:20:16,610 --> 00:20:18,990
I'll make her easier to move, then.

307
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:24,170
She's too big right now.

308
00:20:36,490 --> 00:20:38,050
She's getting smaller!

309
00:20:38,660 --> 00:20:43,770
<i>This light... Aether? 
So he's a Divine Knight too?</i>

310
00:20:44,330 --> 00:20:49,260
<i>But the Goddess' blessing 
is needed to create a Divine Knight.</i>

311
00:20:49,730 --> 00:20:53,430
<i>I thought I couldn't sense her 
in this world...</i>

312
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:56,690
<i>Is there a divine existence here after all?</i>

313
00:21:00,350 --> 00:21:03,040
The aether in her body is gone,

314
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:06,320
so returning her to her original size 
will be almost impossible.

315
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:13,090
But that also means that she can never again 
grow large enough to be a threat to others.

316
00:21:13,420 --> 00:21:17,870
I hate to say it, but I couldn't do 
what you've done right now.

317
00:21:17,870 --> 00:21:20,580
Keep your promise, then. Go.

318
00:21:21,700 --> 00:21:23,800
What about the people 
in the castle and the town?

319
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:25,800
We won't hurt them.

320
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:28,290
Our only enemy are the Highlanders.

321
00:21:29,450 --> 00:21:31,880
I believe you.

322
00:21:38,550 --> 00:21:40,360
Lady Seilyn!

323
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:41,640
Don't go!

324
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:43,980
Lady Seilyn!

325
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:48,170
She'll come back someday.

326
00:21:48,170 --> 00:21:49,360
Really?

327
00:21:49,360 --> 00:21:53,350
Yup. So all of you, 
stay friends with each other!

328
00:21:53,350 --> 00:21:57,200
So that when she comes back, 
she'll be happy.

329
00:21:57,900 --> 00:21:58,910
Okay...

330
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:04,550
Bye-bye, Lady Seilyn!

331
00:22:04,550 --> 00:22:07,300
Come back, okay?

332
00:22:05,860 --> 00:22:09,020
We'll be waiting!

333
00:22:13,990 --> 00:22:14,940
Hey!

334
00:22:15,290 --> 00:22:20,070
Lady Seilyn, stop moving 
around like that! It tickles!

335
00:22:27,200 --> 00:22:31,250
She's so cute after the ice melted!

336
00:22:33,300 --> 00:22:35,770
Rani, please...

337
00:22:35,770 --> 00:22:38,850
Well, mine are too small.

338
00:22:38,850 --> 00:22:41,700
She seems to like your breasts better.

339
00:22:42,080 --> 00:22:43,960
Right, Lyn?

340
00:22:45,760 --> 00:22:46,840
Lyn?

341
00:22:47,710 --> 00:22:52,880
She's so small now! So I thought "Lyn" 
fit better than calling her "Lady Seilyn."

342
00:22:52,880 --> 00:22:55,080
Lyn, come on outside...

343
00:22:57,130 --> 00:22:59,480
Stop moving around!

344
00:23:01,660 --> 00:23:03,700
What's wrong, Rani?

345
00:23:03,700 --> 00:23:10,940
I still don't know who was right 
and who was wrong this time.

346
00:23:10,940 --> 00:23:15,480
The Bloodchain Brigade said they 
were trying to protect the town.

347
00:23:15,480 --> 00:23:17,020
Yup.

348
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:20,730
It just makes my head hurt!

349
00:23:20,730 --> 00:23:22,570
That's just part of being young.

350
00:23:23,040 --> 00:23:24,970
No, I don't think so...

351
00:23:24,970 --> 00:23:27,060
It doesn't bother you, Chris?

352
00:23:27,060 --> 00:23:28,960
Yup. 'Cause I don't think about it.

353
00:23:29,440 --> 00:23:34,110
As long as you only think about 
getting stronger, it won't bother you.

354
00:23:34,110 --> 00:23:35,600
Want to try it, Rani?

355
00:23:36,650 --> 00:23:38,470
I'll pass.

356
00:23:38,470 --> 00:23:40,300
Then think about it all you like.

357
00:23:40,300 --> 00:23:42,670
I'm always on your side, okay?

358
00:23:42,670 --> 00:23:44,660
Yeah, thanks!

359
00:23:45,860 --> 00:23:50,850
Do something!

360
00:23:45,860 --> 00:23:50,850
Paradise

361
00:23:45,860 --> 00:23:50,850
Comic by Kuromura Moto

